1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,340
一 二 三
One, two, three!

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,520
大家好 我们来了
Hey, guys! We're here!

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:05,828
欢迎
Welcome!

4
00:00:05,828 --> 00:00:08,440
泳池很爽 厨房有小吃
Pool's cool, snacks in the kitchen,

5
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,200
我喝了些葡萄酒
I've had some rosé,

6
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,240
开启米奇尔欢乐模式
so fun Mitchell is in the house.

7
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:13,000
大秀美腿
Showing quite a bit of leg.

8
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:14,840
-可真是 -像世界杯比赛一样吗
- This is very... ? - World-cuppy?

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,140
他们来了
There they are!

10
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:20,200
啃老啃了我将近50年的
My adult children still sponging off me

11
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,380
-成年子女 -真"好笑"啊
- after nearly five decades. - Love it.

12
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:24,700
抱歉 原想开个玩笑 没想到道出了残酷的真相
Sorry, thought I'd bend that into a joke, but it stayed real.

13
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,460
-孩子们 -你好 外公
- Hi, kids! - Hey, Grandpa.

14
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,440
菲尔
Hey, Phil.

15
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,320
他这是闹哪出
What's up his can?

16
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:34,960
我不知道
I don't know.

17
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,300
这年头当白人太不容易了
Not easy being a white man these days.

18
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:38,660
你懂的
You feel me.

19
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:41,720
我准备了给老爸和歌洛莉亚的周年礼物
So, I got Dad and Gloria's anniversary present.

20
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:43,138
你们都欠我40块
You guys both owe me 40 bucks.

21
00:00:43,138 --> 00:00:44,283
等等 今天是他们的结婚纪念日
Wait. It's their anniversary?

22
00:00:44,283 --> 00:00:46,060
我以为是歌洛莉亚的生日
I-I thought it was Gloria's birthday.

23
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:47,580
不可能是她生日
Oh, it can't be Gloria's birthday.

24
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,180
一提到生日她就抓狂
She gets mad even if you mention it.

25
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,550
我曾经问过她日期
I once asked when it was,

26
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,031
她就在我包里塞了个肢解的贝兹娃娃
and she left a dismembered Bratz doll in my purse.

27
00:00:54,475 --> 00:00:55,540
今天到底是什么日子
Then why are we here?

28
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:58,100
算了 我去看看蛋糕上写的什么
You know what? I'm gonna go check what the cake says.

29
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,060
给我也来杯"蛋糕"吧
Oh, I'll have a glass of "Cake," Too.

30
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:00,600
没问题
Okay.

31
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,280
趁她不在 给我点情感建议
Quick, before she comes back, I need some relationship advice,

32
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:05,200
这算是道德伦理上是灰色区域
and this is kind of in a gray area ethically.

33
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,500
所以问我们就没事
Oh, and it's okay to ask us

34
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,140
谁让我们基佬的生活如此离经叛道
because, as gays, we wouldn't dare judge anyone

35
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:10,149
哪有资格去评判别人
while living such a deviant lifestyle?

36
00:01:10,149 --> 00:01:13,140
就算基佬界最美的爱情故事和你们直男直女
Even the most beautiful version of our love is a mortal stain

37
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,780
做出的最肮脏的事相比 也是个道德污点
compared to the worst thing you could do?

38
00:01:15,034 --> 00:01:16,459
我还是找别人谈谈吧
Maybe I should talk to somebody else.

39
00:01:16,459 --> 00:01:18,160
-别 告诉我们 -别啊 快说
- No, tell us! - No! Spill, girl, spill!

40
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,860
不许说出去
Okay, so just between us,

41
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,810
我现在和阿尔文在一起 他去瑞士工作了
you know I'm with Arvin and he's working in Switzerland.

42
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:23,291
我干了件坏事
Well, I did something bad.

43
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,140
我亲了迪兰
I kissed Dylan.

44
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,618
迪兰还没走啊
Whoa, Dylan's still around?

45
00:01:27,618 --> 00:01:29,540
我以为他加入了个邪教什么的
I-I thought he joined a cult or something.

46
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:31,660
我听说他把曼妥思和可乐混吃然后自爆了
I heard he ate Mentos and a Coke and exploded.

47
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,720
我也不知道为什么亲他 那个吻没有意义
I don't know why I did it. It meant nothing,

48
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,780
现在很后悔 阿尔文一直在给我打电话
but I feel horrible, and Arvin keeps calling,

49
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,240
我一直没接 因为...
but I'm not picking up because, like --

50
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:38,660
我一定要告诉他吗
Do I have to tell him?

51
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:42,160
亲爱的 每段感情都会经历这种事
Uh, uh, honey, these things happen in every relationship.

52
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:44,798
完全不用什么事都告诉对方
You absolutely do not need to tell your partner everything.

53
00:01:44,798 --> 00:01:46,948
听自己的老公说这话可真有趣
Okay, well, that's a fun thing to hear your husband say.

54
00:01:46,948 --> 00:01:48,760
得了吧 不要小题大做
Oh, please, do not turn this into something.

55
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,860
我本来想说的是 没错 你应该告诉阿尔文
Well, I was going to say, yes, you need to tell Arvin

56
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,779
感情需要建立在真实之上
because you want your relationship based on truth,

57
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:54,389
很明显我的就没有
which, apparently, mine is not.

58
00:01:54,389 --> 00:01:56,240
糟透了 到底该怎么办
Ugh, this sucks! I don't know what to do.

59
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,900
我还指望至少你们能意见一致呢
I was counting on you two to be on the same page.

60
00:01:57,980 --> 00:02:00,000
-通常都意见一致 -我们什么时候意见一致过
- Well, we usually are. - When have you ever seen that?

61
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,720
你们几个小野鸡在叨些什么呢
What are you hens cackling about?

62
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,360
就一般的寒暄问暖
Oh, just asking how they are.

63
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:04,957
我去泳池玩玩
Gonna jump in the pool.

64
00:02:04,957 --> 00:02:06,260
好吧 再会
Okay, see you.

65
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,840
海莉才不关心别人的生活
Haley doesn't care how people are.

66
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,720
-到底怎么了 -没什么
- What's going on? - It's nothing.

67
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,680
她就是来取取经
She was just asking for some advice.

68
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,220
那她干嘛不找我呢
Why wouldn't she come to me?

69
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:15,339
我还以为我们终于要变成知心好友了
I thought we were finally becoming friends.

70
00:02:15,339 --> 00:02:17,040
你自己想想 克莱尔
Well, you know, think about it, Claire.

71
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,060
你瞒着你妈多少事
All the secrets that you kept from your mom.

72
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,100
好吧 但我老妈
Yeah, but my mom

73
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,520
是个保守的疯女人
was an uptight, crazy person.

74
00:02:22,914 --> 00:02:26,182
慢慢向后退 别惊动她
Let's just slowly back away as that settles in.

75
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:44,420
嘿 伙计
Hey, buddy!

76
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:47,860
准备享受前所未有的味觉之...
Ready for the best thing to happen to your mouth since --

77
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:48,800
编不下去了
I'm gonna bail on that.

78
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:50,360
我还没想好就脱口而出了
I took off without a place to land.

79
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,634
-来杯"薄荷杰丽普酒"吧 -不了吧
- How about a Mint "Jay-lep"? - I'll pass,

80
00:02:52,634 --> 00:02:55,212
鉴于我不是个一百岁的南方老太太
seeing as I'm not a hundred-year-old Southern lady.

81
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,880
我终于看完了电影《贱女孩》
I finally saw the movie "Mean Girls."

82
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:01,540
我懂 我都是个中年油腻大叔了
I know. I'm a middle-aged man.

83
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:02,860
我怎么到现在才看
How'd I wait so long?

84
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:06,300
重点是 我发现身边也有个"贱女孩"
The point is, I realized I have a mean girl in my life --

85
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:07,420
就是杰
Jay.

86
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:08,920
比如在上周的婚礼上
Like last week at this wedding,

87
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:10,739
我在耍太空步 杰大喊
I'm rocking my moonwalk, and Jay yells,

88
00:03:10,739 --> 00:03:13,658
"快看 是迈克尔·抽筋逊"
"Hey, look, it's Michael Jerkson."

89
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,140
实在忍无可忍了
Enough's enough.

90
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:18,000
怎样才能让"贱女孩"嘴别那么贱了
How do you get a mean girl to stop being a mean girl?

91
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:20,689
就是嘴比他更贱
Be mean girlier.

92
00:03:20,761 --> 00:03:22,426
不 不 不 不 你会喜欢的
No, no, no, no, you're gonna love it.

93
00:03:22,426 --> 00:03:24,226
薄荷杰丽普非常流行
Mint Jay-leps are all the rage.

94
00:03:24,226 --> 00:03:26,242
你一直在说"薄荷杰丽普"
Oh, you keep saying "Jay-leps."

95
00:03:26,242 --> 00:03:29,438
我调了薄荷朱丽普酒 然后我的名字是杰
Yeah, well I made juleps, and -- and -- and my name's Jay,

96
00:03:29,438 --> 00:03:31,020
所以就叫"薄荷杰丽普"
so I call them "Jay-leps."

97
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:32,320
不 我懂的
No, I get it.

98
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:35,360
这样很好玩啊
It's just a fun thing.

99
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:38,058
这就是让我们久仰大名的薄荷杰丽普吗
Ooh, are these the Mint Jay-leps we've been hearing about?

100
00:03:38,058 --> 00:03:39,880
-没错 -薄荷杰丽普
- Yeah. - Oh, Jay-leps.

101
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,300
-真可爱 -是很可爱
- Adorbs. - They are adorbs.

102
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:42,820
我为何要质疑自己
Why do I doubt myself?

103
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:44,160
曼尼
Manny!

104
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,858
公路旅行如何
How was the road trip?

105
00:03:45,858 --> 00:03:48,860
怎么说呢 为期六周 跨越33个州
Uh, what can I say? Six weeks, 33 states,

106
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:51,120
很多小货车的后面都吊着一个假阴囊
a lot of fake scrotums on the back of pickup trucks.

107
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,220
他遇到了一个非常棒的女朋友
And he met a very nice girlfriend,

108
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,320
现在坠入了爱河
and he's in love.

109
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,000
看看照片
Let's see a pic.

110
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:56,878
我也希望有
Wish I could.

111
00:03:56,878 --> 00:03:59,100
我用的是老式胶片摄像机
I-I went old-school and used a film camera,

112
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,340
她的照片胶卷不慎掉入了大峡谷
and the one roll I took of her fell into the Grand Canyon.

113
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:03,360
你连一张照片都没有
You don't have a single photo of her?

114
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,000
手机上有张很模糊的
Uh, well, just this blurry one on my phone.

115
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,140
拿来看看
Oh, let's see.

116
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:08,160
快看
Look at her.

117
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,900
虽然看不清她的脸
You can't really make her out,

118
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,420
但还是能感受到她放荡不羁的灵魂
but it captures her wild spirit.

119
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:11,900
没错
Yes.

120
00:04:14,852 --> 00:04:16,880
-是我瞎还是曼尼确实爱上了大脚怪 -是啊
- Is it me, or is Manny dating Bigfoot? - Yeah.

121
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,540
我来告诉你们曼尼的女朋友
Let me tell you the difference

122
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,200
和大脚怪的区别
between Manny's girlfriend and Bigfoot.

123
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,040
大脚怪有可能是真的
Bigfoot could be real.

124
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,500
她不是虚构女友
She's not a fake girlfriend.

125
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,420
想知道致命一击是什么吗
You want to hear the kicker?

126
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,078
她来自加拿大
She's from Canada.

127
00:04:26,078 --> 00:04:27,805
-不要啊 -要命了
- Oh, no. - Oh, yikes.

128
00:04:27,805 --> 00:04:30,418
-别这样 -孩子们 支持我
- Oh, stop it! - Back me up, boys.

129
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:31,580
歌洛莉亚 你知道吗
You know what, Gloria?

130
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,580
加拿大有很多好的方面
Canada is good for a lot of things,

131
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,220
但他们最大的出口品就是虚构女友
but their number-one export is fake girlfriends.

132
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,760
没错 基本已经形成共识了
Yeah, it's kind of a thing.

133
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:41,060
小卡和我出柜前 也各自有过加拿大女友
Uh, before Cam and I came out, we each had Canadian girlfriends.

134
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,200
你们想说什么 曼尼是同性恋吗
So, what are you saying now? That Manny's gay?

135
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:47,620
我们可没这么说 但他确实符合一些特征
We weren't, but he does check a few of the boxes.

136
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:49,340
拜托 看看他
Come on. Look at him.

137
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:52,900
他和从卡塔赫纳游到休斯顿的偷渡线路一样直
He's as straight as the swim from Cartagena to Houston.

138
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,760
旅途棒极了 我做了最调皮的事
The trip was amazing, and I did the cheekiest thing.

139
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,480
我在俄克拉荷马州看了《俄克拉荷马》
I saw "Oklahoma!" In Oklahoma,

140
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,440
在芝加哥看了《芝加哥》 然后
"Chicago" In Chicago, and then,

141
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,340
我在河畔城遇上了些小麻烦
I got in a little trouble in River City.

142
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:04,300
够了 那是我听过的最基的事了
Okay, that's the gayest thing I've ever heard,

143
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,960
我可是在西好莱坞做过狗狗美容师
and I shampooed dogs in West Hollywood.

144
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,780
他交过很多女朋友
He's had so many girlfriends.

145
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,440
上一个是20多岁的成熟女性
The last one was a woman in her 20s.

146
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,680
但你不是说过 当她来留宿时
Yeah, but didn't you say he was so sweet when she stayed over

147
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,800
他总是很贴心地主动睡沙发
he offered to sleep on the couch?

148
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:14,880
那又怎样
So what?

149
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:17,000
我的第一个男友就和他同龄
My first boyfriend at his age,

150
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:18,740
他也没准备好和我上床
he wasn't ready to sleep with me.

151
00:05:19,180 --> 00:05:20,040
那他现在怎么样了
And what does he do now?

152
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,960
他开了一家很温馨的民宿旅馆
He runs a very nice bed and breakfast.

153
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:24,800
-和... -和...
- With...? - With...?

154
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,380
和他的好朋友斯蒂文一起
His good friend Steven!

155
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:27,820
闭嘴
Shut up!

156
00:05:29,479 --> 00:05:33,608
如果曼尼背着这样的秘密 那我真的很同情他
I-I really feel for Manny if he's wrestling with this secret.

157
00:05:33,608 --> 00:05:37,260
但你却不介意16年来对我隐瞒你不忠的秘密
Yet you had no problem keeping an indiscretion from me for 16 years.

158
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:38,580
-又开始了 -没错
- And off we go. - Yeah.

159
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:40,480
就像那天给你送了两个包裹的
Just like the shorts of that beefy UPS driver

160
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,020
健壮快递员的短裤
that delivered you two packages that day.

161
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:44,140
事情不是那样的
Wow, that is not what happened!

162
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:45,920
所以你承认有事发生过
So, you admit something happened!

163
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:47,220
好吧 我会全部告诉你
Okay, I'm gonna tell you everything

164
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,320
因为事情比你脑补的要无害多了
'cause it is so much tamer than what's in your head.

165
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,460
-好啊 -我们开始交往后六周
- Okay. - Six weeks into our relationship,

166
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:53,300
在我们确定专一关系前
before we decided we were exclusive,

167
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:55,960
我在酒吧亲了一个人
I kissed someone in a bar.

168
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:58,500
-根本不严重 -很严重好吗
- See, it's not a big deal. - Okay, yes, it is a big deal,

169
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:03,220
正因此 同一时期 我才会拒绝了
which is why I rejected a very similar advance at the same time

170
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,260
一个名人的追求
from a celebrity,

